{
	"id": "errors-compose",
	"text": "Let's see what happens when we add a second failure case. I've always found 6 to be rather bumptious. So whenever it is rolled, the effect will fail with TooHigh. The very moment we update our code, the type changes. The error type becomes the union of all possible failures, perfectly modeling the actual runtime behavior of our program.",
	"code": "const slowDie: Effect.Effect<number, VeryBadRoll> =\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const n = yield* Random.nextIntBetween(1, 7)\n    yield* Effect.sleep(\"1 second\")\n    if (n === 4) yield* Effect.fail(new VeryBadRoll())\n    return n\n  })",
	"contentHash": "kaaqzo",
